        "id": "synth_step_1",
        "type": "synthesis",
        "name": "Nanoparticle Deposition",
        "procedure": "Mass-selected nanoparticles (4-8 nm in diameter) of a metallic Ni–Fe alloy are deposited onto a clean and smooth gold disk in vacuum by magnetron sputtering. By transmission electron microscopy the particles are found to be uniform polycrystalline spheres. Because of how the catalyst is deposited, the authors can quantify accurately the catalyst mass loading as well as the surface area of the initial metal particles.",
        "unit_operations": [
          {
