        "source_text": "They deposit mass-selected nanoparticles (4-8 nm in diameter) of a metallic Ni–Fe alloy onto a clean and smooth gold disk in vacuum by magnetron sputtering. By transmission electron microscopy the particles are found to be uniform polycrystalline spheres."
